 "notes": "Recall only: the spec covers /api/v2, served by the go-swagger generated server (api/v2/restapi) mounted with mux.Handle(apiPrefix+\"/api/v2/\", ...) in api/api.go — nothing under api/v2/ registered routes the extractor could see (generated-server) until H2b's generated servers (2026-10-16): o.handlers[\"GET\"][\"/alerts\"] in restapi/operations, under the basePath that restapi/embedded_spec.go embeds; since then all 9 come out. The other routes of the repo (v1 deprecation, /-/healthy, ui) are not in the spec, so precision comes from the manual sample. Precision: all 22 extracted routes checked. The 7 v1 routes are registered on r.WithPrefix(\"/api/v1\") passed into V1DeprecationRouter.Register and come out without the prefix (router-as-param); DELETE /api/v1/silence/:sid uses r.Del (verb-alias) and is missed. Also missed outside the spec: GET / (ui/web.go — a path with no literal segment is dropped) and GET /ui/ (normalized into /ui, merged). Calls: the notifiers take the host from config and append a literal path to a net/url value (u.Path += \"v2/alerts\", fmt.Sprintf into .Path, APIURL.JoinPath(\"api/v1/chat.postMessage\")) and send u.String() later — none extracted until H2b's Go calls (2026-10-16, url-object-builder); since then all but rocketchat's, which posts through a function kept in a struct field (n.postJSONFunc, set to notify.PostJSON: client-in-field). The go-swagger client in api/v2/client declares each operation in a runtime.ClientOperation{Method, PathPattern}: its 9 operations are expected calls with the path as declared (the spec's basePath /api/v2 is added by the transport, like a base URL). Measured on opsgenie, wechat and rocketchat, where method and path are unambiguous; jira does the same with JoinPath(\"/search\") and issue/{key}/transitions. Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15): the mux.Handle(prefix+\"/api/v1/\", ...) subtree mounts are no longer routes (they were judged right in v1 as catch-all routes; v2 counts them as mounts, mount-as-route).",
